WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.570
-Our next guest
is a 10-time Grammy winner

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.971
and Country Music Hall of Famer.

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:07.206
This is his new book here,

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:09.575
"Willie Nelson's
Letters to America,"

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.844
which comes out June 29th.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:14.480
Here is the one and only
Willie Nelson.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.015
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.716
That's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:19.919
Looking great, buddy.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.588
Willie, I love you.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.722
Welcome back, pal.

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.792
-Thank you, Jimmy.
It's good to be back.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.227
-In August,
you're about to kick off

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.329
the Outlaw Music Festival Tour.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:31.664
You're back on tour.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.133
Are you excited?

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.202
-Yeah, I'm glad to,
you know, get back out.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.670
It's been over a year now,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:41.374
and I'm not sure I can remember
"Whiskey River."

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:44.077
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.513
Well, of course, the first thing
that a lot of people think of

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:50.549
when they think of you going on
tour is "On the Road Again."

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:52.418
And I didn't want to do that.
It could be too corny.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.420
But, I do love that,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.889
and we all love you singing
"On the Road Again."

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:59.058
Do you remember writing
"On the Road Again"

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:01.528
and where did that come from?

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.163
-Yeah, I was on an airplane

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:07.000
with Sydney Pollack
and Jerry Schatzberg,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.670
the director of and producer

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.105
of the "Honeysuckle Rose" movie.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:15.408
-Yeah.
-And they were trying

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:19.545
to think of a song
that might go with the movie.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:22.248
And I said, "Well, what do you
want the song to be like,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.317
or what do you want it to say?"

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.687
And they said, "Well, something
about being on the road."

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.555
And I said, "Well,
what about on the road again,

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.090
I can't wait to get
on the road again,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.425
the life I love
is making music with my friends,

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.094
I can't wait
to get on the road again --

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.262
Is that alright?"

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.598
And they said,
"I think so, yeah."

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.267
-[ Laughs ]
"That's exactly it. Yes.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.170
Did we record that?
Yes, that's it.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.206
Do it three more times,
we got a song."

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.442
Happy birthday, by the way.
I know you're --

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.544
You're 88, is that correct?

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.346
-88.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:55.381
88.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.982 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:02.588
-Is there a secret
that keeps you going strong?

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:06.859
-Oh, I think, you know, you got
to keep a positive attitude.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:09.028
I believe that.
I always have believed that.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.598
In fact, I wrote a new song
the other day --

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:15.601
"Imagine what you want,
and then get out of the way."

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:20.006
And I think the most important
line is "get out of the way."

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.641
-Yeah, like -- I like that.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.675
[ Applause ]

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.543
Imagine --

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.045
Were you always into that,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:30.583
like, into visualization
or visualizing your future?

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.852
-Yeah.
Maybe I did it a long time

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.154
without realizing
what I was doing.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:38.558
But someone told me
one time that --

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.893
this was the
Norman Vincent Peale, I think,

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.329
and some of those guys
he talked about --

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.164
Power of positive thinking.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.266
And I began to realize

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.368
that there was
a lot of truth in that.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:52.838
-Yeah. During this time

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:56.409
that we all stayed in at home
and didn't leave,

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.811
not only did you
write a great book,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:03.116
but you also did a duet
with Barbra Streisand.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.150
-Yeah.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.485
-I loved it, by the way.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:08.721
I can't believe you guys
have never sang together.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.591
-Well, matter of fact, we did --
Years ago, we did a song.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.292
It never came out.

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:16.362
But then she asked me
to do this one.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:20.299
And, you know, she's always been
one of my favorite people,

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:21.800
a great singer.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.871
We had a lot of fun
hanging out with her

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:28.240
back when they were doing
"A Star is Born"

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.875
with Kris Kristofferson.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.143
-Wow.
-And, you know,

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:32.812
we became good friends,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.880
so I was glad
to be able to sing with her.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.982
She's -- She's a great singer,

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:40.886
and one of my desires
was to do a duet with Barbra.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:42.021
-Yeah, it's fantastic.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.756
And her record
comes out pretty soon.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.758
But she'll be
on the show for that.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:50.062
I got to say, reading this book,
it's like hanging out with you,

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.830
what I believe would be
hanging out with you.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.599
You don't allow me
to hang out with you. But --

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:54.833
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:58.104
But if I could,
I'd bet it would be like this.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.806
I just want to read
just the first sentence of this.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.708
The introduction's like,
"Dear readers,

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.710
thank you for picking up a copy
of my new book,

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.480
a collection of fond memories,
personal letters,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.449
good songs, and bad jokes."

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.949
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:12.585
That is exactly the vibe,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.621
and it is so cool and so funny
and so interesting.

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:18.290
You go into --
You do tell jokes in here.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:22.395
You go into some snippets
of songs that you're writing,

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.096
brand-new songs
that you're writing.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:28.534
What made you
want to write this?

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.637
-Oh, I don't know. Somebody
said something about money.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.506
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.141
[ Applause ]

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:42.815 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:50.489 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:53.592
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:55.728
Really, I thought
it was a good idea,

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.463
and Turk Pipkin and I --

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.032
the writer
who helped me with the book,

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.567
a great friend of mine,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.636
and we've done, you know, a lot
of things together in the past.

00:05:04.636 --> 00:05:06.239
So I had a lot of fun doing it.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:08.241
-Well, next time
I see you in-person,

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.508
I would love for you
to sign my copy,

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.010
'cause I'm going to read it
every single day

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.177
until I see you.
-I would.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:13.646
-Willie Nelson, everybody.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:18.551
His book "Letters to America,"
comes out June 29th.

